\title{Binomial heap}
\date{2026-11-21T19:34:16Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{A \em{binomial heap} is a list of [binomial trees](00TG) such that:
\ul{
  \li{Each binomial tree satisfies the heap property (the value stored at each node is smaller than all its children)}
  \li{There is at most one binomial tree of any given order.}
}
}

\p{Below is an example of a valid binomial heap.}

\diagram{500}{*}{\verb<<<|
import BinomialHeaps

dia = drawBinomialHeap drawNode goodBinomialHeap # frame 1
<<<}
